!#!Info  Beispiel:      Taktschieben im Bogen 2
!#!Info  Schlagwort:    Taktschieben; Moving spring
!#!Info  Program:       CSM


$ Bitte beachten Sie auch : CSM Handbuch:  Theoretische Grundlagen - Taktschieben Schulung

$ Animation:
$ - Bitte den Animator mit dem ersten BA-Lastfall 4100 starten,
$ - die Amplitude auf einen festen Wert einstellen (Button)
$ - klicken ins Feld 'Überhöhung' und z.B. 20 eintippen
$ - das Animationstempo auf 0 stellen (0 eintippen oder \textcolor[rgb]{1,0,0}{rote Hand})
$ - dann die 4000-er Lastfälle durchblättern.
$ Hierzu können die Tastatur-Cursortaste Cursor-down (Pfeil nach unten)
$ verwendet werden, wenn man in der Lastfall-Dialogbox einen Lastfall ausgewählt hat.
$ Evtl. ist die Verwendung der Lastfallschleife sinnvoll (mit speed>0).

!#!Kapitel System
+PROG AQUA URS:1
KOPF Taktschieben im Bogen 2
NORM  'DIN' 'en199X-200X-BRIDGE'     CAT 'B'
UNIT 5 $ Einheiten: Querschnitte in mm, Geometrie+Lasten in m
!*!Label Material
BETO  1    C    40        $ = C40/50
STAH  2                   $ standard reinforcement steel 500
STAH  9    S  '235' $ structural steel for tubes, rolled steel ...
STAH 99    S  '235' TMAX 0 GAM 0 ES 900000 $ coupling beams
STAH 11    Y '1860A' $ prestessing steel
                    $ fp0,1k = 1600 N/mm2
                    $ fpk    = 1860 N/mm2
                    $            0.8*fpk    = 0.80*1860 = 1488 N/mm2
                    $            0.9*fp0,1k = 0.90*1600 = 1440 N/mm2
                    $ sigp,max = min(1488,1440)         = 1440 N/mm2 EN-1992-1-1 5.10.2.1(1) maximale Spannung
                    $ sigp,SLS = 0.65*fpk   = 0.65*1860 = 1209 N/mm2 EN-1992-1-1 7.2(5)      bei Verkehrsübergabe quasiständig
                    $ sigp,rare= sigp,max

!*!Label  Section 1
QNR  1 MNR 1
sto#zmax 1860
QPOL  UPZ MNR 1
QP -  0    0
   - 3280
   - 3330  200
   - 1600  350
   - 1680 1140
   - 1650 1160
   - 1600 #zmax
QPOL  UPZ MNR 0
QP -  0  280
   - 1150  380
   - 1150 1620
$
$  Torsion box:  *---------------------> y
$                |
$     *----------|----------*     #zo
$     |          |<---#yo-->|
$     |          |          |
$     |          |          |
$     |          |<---#yu-->|
$     *----------|----------*     #zu
$                z
let#yo  1500 $ [mm] y-Wert der Torsionsbox oben
let#yu  1500 $ [mm] y-Wert der Torsionsbox unten
let#zo    60 $ [mm] z-Wert der Torsionsbox oben
let#zu #zmax-60 $ " der Torsionsbox unten  "       of Torsionsbox below
LBEW  1 #yo #zo   #yu  #zu AS 1 RANG 0 TORS AKTI D  12
LBEW  2   -   -  -#yu  #zu AS 1 RANG 0 TORS AKTI D  12
LBEW  3   -   -  -#yo  #zo AS 1 RANG 0 TORS AKTI D  12
LBEW  4   -   -   #yo  #zo AS 1 RANG 0 TORS AKTI D  12
let#yo 3200     $ y Biegebewehrung oben
let#yu #yu-50   $ unten
LBEW  5 #yu #zu-50 -#yu  AS     - RANG 1       TORS PASS D  20
LBEW  6 #yo #zo+50 -#yo  AS     - RANG 2       TORS PASS D  20
QS 1 ZA 400     MNR 1
QS 2 ZA 600     MNR 1
QSP    NR    Y    Z     MNR
     'UMI'   0  #zmax   1 $ Literal BOT muss in Grossbuchstaben eingegeben werden
     'OMI'   0    0     1
loop#i0 11
  let#i1 #i0+1
  let#h 1800-120*#i0
  QNR 100+#i1 MNR 9 BEZ 'launching nose #h'
    QSP 'TOPL' Y -600 Z #zmax-#h ; QSP 'TOPR' Y +600 Z #zmax-#h $ #zmax from main section 1
    QSP 'BOTL' Y -600 Z #zmax    ; QSP 'BOTR' Y +600 Z #zmax
      BLEC REFA REFE   D=8 YA=0 ZA=0 YE=0 ZE=0
           'TOPL' 'TOPR'
           'TOPR' 'BOTR'
           'BOTR' 'BOTL'
           'BOTL' 'TOPL'
endloop

QC 91 D 1500[mm] MNR 1 $ Pfeiler
QC 97 D  10[mm] T 0.01[mm] MNR 99 BEZ 'Launching rail' $ 0.01 mm to get small area and small normalforce in rail !
QC 98 D 250[mm]  MNR 99 BEZ 'to avoid spreading'
QC 99 D 1500[mm] T 50[mm]  MNR 99 BEZ 'coupling beams'
ENDE

+PROG SOFIMSHC URS:3 $ Definition of the main axis, spans, main beam and axis variables
KOPF Taktschieben im Bogen 2
UNIT 5 $ Einheiten: Querschnitte in mm, Geometrie+Lasten in m
SYST RAUM GDIV 1000 POSZ
sto#R 304.155 $m radius

$ As this span definition is used often in the file, it is defined once and stored:
STO#S_XI(99)  0     $ allocate table
STO#S_XI(0)   0.00  $ start of bridge at left excess  -   am linken Überstand
STO#S_XI(1)   1.00  $ first support                   -   erstes Lager
STO#S_XI(2)  42.00  $ 2.    support                   -   2.     Lager
STO#S_XI(3)  94.00  $ 3.    support                   -   3.     Lager
STO#S_XI(4) 146.00  $ 4.    support                   -   3.     Lager
STO#S_XI(5) 198.00  $ 4.    support                   -   3.     Lager
STO#S_XI(6) 240.00  $ 4.    support                   -   3.     Lager
STO#S_XI(7) 241.00  $ end of bridge at right excess   -   am rechten Überstand
STO#S_XI(8) 271.00  $ end of launching nose           -   Ende Vorbauschnabel
$ an excess is always important - otherwise the bridge may not catch the support while launching!
$
$ now you can access to the table also with interpolation:
$ s at span 2 at local xi=0.6 -> let#s =S_XI(2.6)    gives s back with 42 + 0.6*(94-42)
STO#s_end =S_XI(7.0)  $ for SOFILOAD - end of bridge
TXA Testprint variable s_end =  #(s_end,8.3)   $ (8 characters and 3 digits)


$ ------------------------------------- axis : ------------------------------
GAX 'AX_1'
  GAXA S  0 X 0 -#R 0 SX 1 0 0 $ first starting point with starting direction
  GAXA L 400[m] R #R
$ ------------------------------------- main beam : ------------------------------
STEU MESH 1 ; STEU HMIN 999.0  $ meshing of beam elements 999: all nodes individually set !
$ This is necessary because couplings are not rotated while launched in a circle!
$ So instead of coupling real coupling beams are used!
$ To define these individual beams, individual nodes are set:

GAXP 'AX_1' S (0 48.00 2) TYP 'A' GRP - NRQ - SPT (1 1)  $ Launching bed - Taktkeller Knoten
sto#nbed         24+1 $ number of nodes in launching bed
let#s0 49.00 $ start station of main bridge excess at #S_XI(0)
let#spt 100  $ first node number at this point
                 GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+0.00        TYP 'A' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt $ start main bridge excess  at #S_XI(0)
sto#node(0) #spt
sto#grpcs(5) #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.00) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt $ first main bridge support at #S_XI(1)
sto#node(1) #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.05) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.10) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.15) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.20) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.25) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.30) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.35) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.40) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.45) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.50) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.55) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.60) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.65) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.70) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.75) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.80) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.85) TYP 'S' GRP 5 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
sto#grpcs(4) #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.90) TYP 'S' GRP 4 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(1.95) TYP 'S' GRP 4 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(2.00) TYP 'S' GRP 4 NRQ 1 SPT #spt  $ 2. main bridge support at #S_XI(2)
sto#node(2) #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(2.05) TYP 'S' GRP 4 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(2.10) TYP 'S' GRP 4 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(2.15) TYP 'S' GRP 4 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(2.20) TYP 'S' GRP 4 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(2.25) TYP 'S' GRP 4 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(2.30) TYP 'S' GRP 4 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
let#spt #spt+1 ; GAXP 'AX_1' S #s0+#S_XI(2.35) TYP 'S' GRP 4 NRQ 1 SPT #spt
